/*

I've just got an idea of replacing invoke! and all the operations with a single Vit instruction "StateSwap".
(As state could be the only variable that actually changes over time, and all the objects would just depend on it)

This is horrible
Because I have absolutely no time to think of it enough or implement it.

But this idea for now seems almost like it solves all the problems we could've had
Like "having to describe objects completely separately from the Vals"
So invoke! just means that it depends on the current state
in fact current invoke does just this
We pass the state implicitly
The only possible issue with StateSwap is that I need to think through how we can make it so "Swapping a state" from which
program started wouldn't take more memory than it actually need

But all the objects
They'll be just values

Man this is so brilliant I hate it

